From 549b350e6cc25d4a9330b73adcf74ff886e271ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDP Mission Control Lab <lab@dictationb1.local>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:26:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0003 R2: bounded WebSocket worker runspace (accept-loop
 starvation repair)

Move only the long-lived /ws pump off the single accept thread onto a
bounded runspace pool gated by a non-blocking SemaphoreSlim. Ordinary HTTP
stays inline so all script-scope ticket/cache/credential state keeps its
single-threaded semantics. At capacity the server answers 503 immediately;
the accept loop never parks. Workers receive only the pump's small
dependency surface, serialize audits on a shared Monitor lock, and release
the gate and close the socket in finally. Pool and semaphore are disposed
at shutdown. Includes the static r2-websocket-worker smoke regression.
